    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_6cc8363bcb3f4f57e69b22aba38ed537a9ad6642f6158a0134b79aff26c2c2e6",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The span turns the cubic family values L(s, chi_D)^3, indexed by fundamental discriminants D, into the coefficients of Z(s,w) = sum_D L(s, chi_D)^3/|D|^w. Introducing w reorganizes dependence on discriminant size into a second complex variable and supplies a prospective analytic handle on cutoff moments, while the definition itself leaves continuation and every asymptotic claim unproved.",
